Where is our help with prescription drug costs, Medicare, and the VA?! I’m a disabled veteran, also on SSDI for Systemic Lupus (SLE) since 2002. My monthly Medicare Rx co-pay for:

💊 Mounjaro (GLP-1): $624.65
💊 Aimovig (Cluster headaches): $550.95
💊 Nurtec (TBI headaches): $618.59 (for 8 pills)

In Jan 2025, Medicare didn’t renew my PPO with United Healthcare and I was forced to select an Aetna PPO which requires that I pay 20% of retail for Tier 3 meds. I pay an extra premium for a PPO, plus a $590 annual Rx deductible. What used to cost me $135.00 under UHC per month, now costs $1,794.19 under Aetna - completely unaffordable!

As a veteran of Desert Shield/Storm you might ask “What about the VA?” So far, I’ve either been denied or told that these medications aren’t in formulary for the VA.

No alternatives. No relief.
@realDonaldTrump 
@AARP
@ChuckGrassley @SenAmyKlobuchar
@SecVetAffairs #MedicareCrisis #DisabilityRights #SLE #VeteransDeserveBetter
